From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:02:28 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 70/92] Plutonium: the lock screen and idle: Ash's own lock
 over every display, Super+L, the idle time, the wake locks and the displays'
 power in the Plutonium domain

EXO-LOCK (docs/features/DESKTOP_SERVICES.md, "session"). In shell mode,
PlutoniumLockImpl draws the lock (the clock, the user's name, a password
field) on every display, in Ash's overlay container, and while it's up
drops every event that isn't for it at Ash's system priority, so nothing
reaches a shell, a tab or an app; the Plutonium keys are off. The helper
checks the password (POST /v1/session/unlock over its socket); only its
yes takes the lock down. Super+L asks the helper to lock
(/v1/session/lock).

The Plutonium domain gets lock, getIdle (locked, the idle time from
ui::UserActivityDetector, the displays' state, the screen wake locks from
PowerPolicyController: video, the Screen Wake Lock API, Wayland idle
inhibitors), setDisplaysOff (DisplayConfigurator on DRM, until the user
does something) and the lockChanged event.
